<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Buying vs Renting</span>
<h1>Teachers: Rent vs Buy Decision for Hanoi Motorbikes</h1>
<p>Teachers in Hanoi eventually meet the same crossroads: whether a motorbike should be owned or rented, and what ownership paperwork actually asks of a foreigner who plans to stay a while and leave again. A teacher's year in Hanoi has a shape, terms, holidays, a summer that may or may not be spent in the city, and the motorbike decision should be made to fit that shape rather than against it. This guide asks the paperwork questions honestly, points every legal and registration answer to current official sources, and never implies that a rental business has bikes for sale, because the desk that rents machines has no stake in anyone buying one.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the staff answer buying-versus-renting questions every day and keep the answer neutral. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-for-sale/">motorbike for sale hub</a>, study the long-stay arrangements on the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly motorbike rental</a> page, and check the verified figures on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, with the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> open for the riding and legal layer.</p>
